Revision history for CryptoKit

0.03    2026-10-23
        - Add CryptoKit::HolopeinenID for self-verifying, time-ordered,
          shard-safe identifiers
        - Add CryptoKit::FileVault for split-and-pack file encryption,
          with both container mode (pack/unpack) and distributed mode
          (split/join)
        - Add CryptoKit::HMAC for HMAC signing with constant-time
          verification
        - Add CryptoKit::TOTP for time-based one-time passwords
        - Add CryptoKit::FileEncrypt for streaming AES-GCM file encryption
        - CryptoKit::Hash: optional HiatalaMrk backend via
          backend => 'hiatala'; verify dispatches on the encoded prefix
          ($argon2id$ vs $hiatalamrk$) so both backends can coexist in the
          same storage column
        - CryptoKit::Password: rewrite to rejection sampling for uniform
          distribution (no modulo bias); roughly 2x faster
        - CryptoKit::FileEncrypt: decrypt seeks to the trailing tag and
          streams from the start, so memory is constant regardless of file
          size (50 MB file previously needed ~120 MB RSS, now ~2 MB)
        - CryptoKit::FileVault: streams chunks one at a time; empty files
          are encoded as a single empty chunk so the manifest's n_chunks
          always matches the records on disk
        - Fix FileVault CORE::pack/CORE::unpack ambiguity warnings
        - Fix HolopeinenID separator (. instead of _) to avoid collision
          with base64url alphabet
        - Expand CLI with verify, hmac, totp, encrypt-file, decrypt-file,
          vault-pack, vault-unpack, hid-issue, hid-verify
        - Add t/perf.t (gated by AUTHOR_TESTING) for baseline benchmarking
        - 15 test files, 95+ subtests

0.02    2026-10-22
        - Add CryptoKit::Encrypt hybrid ECC + AES-GCM
        - Add CryptoKit::Secure wrapper around Crypt::SecretBuffer
        - Add constant-time comparison helpers
        - Add CLI with genpw, hash, keygen
        - Basic tests for hash, password, key, encrypt, secure

0.01    2026-10-22
        - Initial release with CryptoKit::Hash, CryptoKit::Password,
          CryptoKit::Key
        - Argon2id password hashing
        - Strong random password generation
        - ECC key generation and ECDSA sign/verify
